**`{{ .ProjectName }}` [26.10](https://github.com/mariadb-operator/mariadb-operator/releases/tag/26.10.0) is here!** 🦭

First of all, we want to celebrate two amazing milestones that the community has helped us reach: `{{ .ProjectName }}` just crossed **1K stars on GitHub** 🌟 ([mariadb-operator](https://github.com/mariadb-operator/mariadb-operator)) and our **Docker image reached 10M pulls** 📦 ([mariadb-operator](https://github.com/mariadb-operator/mariadb-operator/pkgs/container/mariadb-operator)). This is a testament to the incredible adoption of the project, and we are thrilled to have you on board! If you haven't already, consider starring the repo and telling your peers about it!

Welcome to another release of `{{ .ProjectName }}`! This is a feature-packed one: we are introducing support for **MariaDB 12.3**✨, a series of **replication topology** enhancements, **ZSTD compression** for backups, and several **Galera** improvements.

Additionally, we have received a bunch of contributions from our amazing community during this release, including bug fixes and improvements. We feel very grateful for your efforts and support, thank you! 🙇‍♂️ Refer to the PRs in the changelog below for further details.

If you're upgrading from previous versions, __do not miss the [UPGRADE GUIDE](https://github.com/mariadb-operator/mariadb-operator/blob/main/docs/releases/UPGRADE_26.10.0.md)__ for a smooth transition.

## MariaDB 12.3 support

`{{ .ProjectName }}` now supports **MariaDB 12.3**, the latest long-term support (LTS) release of MariaDB. The default `mariadb` image used by the operator has been bumped to `mariadb:12.3.3`, so new clusters will run on it unless you pin a different image:

```yaml
apiVersion: k8s.mariadb.com/v1alpha1
kind: MariaDB
metadata:
  name: mariadb
spec:
  image: mariadb:12.3.3
  # [...]
```

Existing clusters keep the image pinned in their spec and are not affected by this change.

## Replication topologies

Replication topologies received a series of reliability and correctness improvements in this release:

- The operator no longer issues `RESET MASTER;` when configuring a replica ([#1883](https://github.com/mariadb-operator/mariadb-operator/pull/1883)). Purging a node's binary logs is not required to configure replication, and it is destructive once the node is promoted: its binary log history is gone. This is a key property for [point-in-time recovery](./pitr.md) and [multi-cluster](./multi-cluster.md) topologies.
- Nodes that rejoin the cluster after a hard failover with self-owned GTIDs are now demoted using `MASTER_DEMOTE_TO_SLAVE` ([#1894](https://github.com/mariadb-operator/mariadb-operator/pull/1894)). This non-destructive replacement of `RESET MASTER` unblocks a scenario where a rejoining primary could never converge back to the cluster.
- Switchover no longer leaves the new primary half-configured when clearing `gtid_slave_pos` fails with `Error 1948` ([#1886](https://github.com/mariadb-operator/mariadb-operator/pull/1886)). The new primary's `read_only` state is now properly cleared and its GTID position advances past leftover binary logs, so consecutive switchovers complete as expected.
- The operator now enforces the correct `rpl_semi_sync_master_enabled` state on every node: enabled in the primary and disabled in the replicas ([#1902](https://github.com/mariadb-operator/mariadb-operator/pull/1902)). Previously every node was a semi-synchronous primary, so a replica with `log_slave_updates` enabled could stall writes waiting for a semi-synchronous ACK that can never arrive. A new optional field `replication.semiSyncBootAsReplica` (disabled by default) boots the node `read_only` with the semi-synchronous master disabled, so a node is never writable while it is unable to require a replica acknowledgement.
- A new `replication.semiSyncWaitNoSlave` field exposes `rpl_semi_sync_master_wait_no_slave` for clusters where replicas have no downstream replicas of their own ([#1885](https://github.com/mariadb-operator/mariadb-operator/pull/1885)).
- `read_only` drift on replicas is now corrected even while the replica is unhealthy, as long as the cluster is not attached to MaxScale ([#1884](https://github.com/mariadb-operator/mariadb-operator/pull/1884)).

Refer to the [replication docs](https://github.com/mariadb-operator/mariadb-operator/blob/main/docs/replication.md) for a complete guide.

## ZSTD compression

[Backup](./logical_backup.md), [PhysicalBackup](./physical_backup.md) and [PointInTimeRecovery](./pitr.md) now support `zstd` as a compression algorithm, alongside `none`, `bzip2` and `gzip` ([#1874](https://github.com/mariadb-operator/mariadb-operator/pull/1874)). ZSTD offers an excellent compression/decompression speed with a good compression ratio. A new `compressionThreads` field lets you cap the number of CPU threads used during compression:

```yaml
apiVersion: k8s.mariadb.com/v1alpha1
kind: Backup
metadata:
  name: mariadb-backup
spec:
  compression: zstd
  compressionThreads: 4
  # [...]
```

## Galera improvements

- Logical backups of Galera clusters are now restorable. The dump excludes the Galera-managed `mysql.wsrep_*` system tables, which Galera recreates on bootstrap ([#1836](https://github.com/mariadb-operator/mariadb-operator/pull/1836)).
- Repeatable `mariadb-dump` flags such as `--ignore-table` are no longer silently dropped when passed multiple times, and user-supplied `mariadb-backup` `--databases-exclude` values are now merged with the built-in ones instead of overriding them ([#1836](https://github.com/mariadb-operator/mariadb-operator/pull/1836)).

## Bugfixes

- The replication liveness probe no longer fails (and the Pod no longer restarts) when the replica SQL thread is stopped administratively without error, e.g. during a physical backup with `--safe-slave-backup` ([#1882](https://github.com/mariadb-operator/mariadb-operator/pull/1882))
- `PhysicalBackup` jobs now inherit `podSecurityContext.seLinuxOptions` from the referenced `MariaDB` when the job does not set its own, fixing `Errcode: 13` failures on SELinux-enforced clusters ([#1889](https://github.com/mariadb-operator/mariadb-operator/pull/1889))
- Scheduled `Backup` and `SqlJob` resources now report the `CronJobFailed` condition reason when the last run has failed, instead of `CronJobScheduled` ([#1867](https://github.com/mariadb-operator/mariadb-operator/pull/1867))

## Improvements

- Helm chart releases now include generated release notes, so tools like Renovate and Dependabot can show what changed between chart versions ([#1805](https://github.com/mariadb-operator/mariadb-operator/pull/1805))
- The Helm docs now describe scoping the operator to a specific set of namespaces via `WATCH_NAMESPACE` ([#1868](https://github.com/mariadb-operator/mariadb-operator/pull/1868))
- Bumped the toolchain to Go 1.27 and golangci-lint v2.13.2 ([#1903](https://github.com/mariadb-operator/mariadb-operator/pull/1903))

